<title>BELGIUM: Commission rules against Clabecq aid, newspaper says.</title>
<headline>Commission rules against Clabecq aid, newspaper says.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission has decided that the Belgian government must scrap an aid plan for Belgian steel maker Forges de Clabecq, Belgian daily De Standaard said on Monday.</p>
<p>The paper said that the Commission took its decision last week and that it will be formalised at the Commission's last meeting this year, on December 18.</p>
<p>The Commission said in September that a 1.5 billion franc capital injection together with other measures consisting of a bridging loan and a waiving of claims amounted to state subsidies which can only be allowed under very strict circumstances.</p>
<p>The Commission was not immediately available for comment.</p>
</text>
